Chapter: Sparkplug
  cites Encode chapter Mqtt
  cites Encode chapter Protobuf
  cites Foreword chapter Tuple

 Sparkplug B (Eclipse Sparkplug 3.0) -- the open MQTT specification for
 industrial IoT. A Sparkplug message is an MQTT PUBLISH on a structured
 topic (spBv1.0/group/message-type/edge-node[/device]) carrying a
 Protobuf-encoded Payload of Metrics. This chapter builds both: the
 topic namespace and the payload encoder, layered on the existing Mqtt
 and Protobuf modules.

 Metric values here cover the integer, long, float, double, boolean,
 string, and null datatypes. Float and double use IEEE-754 fixed-width
 encoding (Protobuf fixed32 field 12, fixed64 field 13) via the
 real-approx-to-bits / real-to-bits bitcast intrinsics.

Section: Topic Namespace

  spb-namespace : Text = "spBv1.0"

  spb-msg-nbirth : Text = "NBIRTH"
  spb-msg-ndeath : Text = "NDEATH"
  spb-msg-ndata : Text = "NDATA"
  spb-msg-ncmd : Text = "NCMD"
  spb-msg-dbirth : Text = "DBIRTH"
  spb-msg-ddeath : Text = "DDEATH"
  spb-msg-ddata : Text = "DDATA"
  spb-msg-dcmd : Text = "DCMD"

  spb-node-topic : Text, Text, Text -> Text
  spb-node-topic (group) (msg-type) (node) =
   spb-namespace & "/" & group & "/" & msg-type & "/" & node

  spb-device-topic : Text, Text, Text, Text -> Text
  spb-device-topic (group) (msg-type) (node) (device) =
   spb-node-topic group msg-type node & "/" & device

Section: Data Types

 The Sparkplug metric datatype enumeration (subset).

  spb-dt-int8 : Integer = 1
  spb-dt-int16 : Integer = 2
  spb-dt-int32 : Integer = 3
  spb-dt-int64 : Integer = 4
  spb-dt-uint8 : Integer = 5
  spb-dt-uint16 : Integer = 6
  spb-dt-uint32 : Integer = 7
  spb-dt-uint64 : Integer = 8
  spb-dt-float : Integer = 9
  spb-dt-double : Integer = 10
  spb-dt-boolean : Integer = 11
  spb-dt-string : Integer = 12

Section: Metrics

 A metric carries a name (or an alias, once a birth has established the
 name-to-alias mapping), a datatype, and a value. The Protobuf Metric
 message uses field 1 for name, 2 for alias, 4 for datatype, 7 for the
 is-null flag, and the value fields 10 (int), 11 (long), 12 (float),
 13 (double), 14 (boolean), 15 (string).

  SpbValue =
    | SpbInt (Integer)
    | SpbLong (Integer)
    | SpbFloat (Real approximate)
    | SpbDouble (Real)
    | SpbBool (Boolean)
    | SpbString (Text)
    | SpbNull

  SpbMetric = record {
   name : Text,
   alias : Integer,
   datatype : Integer,
   value : SpbValue
  }

  spb-metric : Text, Integer, SpbValue -> SpbMetric
  spb-metric (name) (datatype) (value) =
   SpbMetric { name = name, alias = 0, datatype = datatype, value = value }

  spb-bdseq-metric : Integer -> SpbMetric
  spb-bdseq-metric (n) =
   SpbMetric { name = "bdSeq", alias = 0, datatype = spb-dt-int64, value = SpbLong n }

  spb-encode-value : SpbValue -> List Integer
  spb-encode-value (v) =
   when v
    is SpbInt (n) -> pb-encode-field-varint 10 n
    is SpbLong (n) -> pb-encode-field-varint 11 n
    is SpbFloat (f) -> pb-encode-field-fixed32 12 (real-approx-to-bits f)
    is SpbDouble (d) -> pb-encode-field-fixed64 13 (real-to-bits d)
    is SpbBool (b) -> pb-encode-field-varint 14 (if b then 1 else 0)
    is SpbString (s) -> pb-encode-field-string 15 s
    is SpbNull -> pb-encode-field-varint 7 1

  spb-encode-metric : SpbMetric -> List Integer
  spb-encode-metric (m) =
   let name-part = if text-length (m.name) > 0 then pb-encode-field-string 1 (m.name) else []
   in let alias-part = if m.alias > 0 then pb-encode-field-varint 2 (m.alias) else []
   in let dt-part = pb-encode-field-varint 4 (m.datatype)
   in name-part & alias-part & dt-part & spb-encode-value (m.value)

Section: Payload

 The Sparkplug Payload: field 1 timestamp, field 2 the repeated metrics
 (each a length-delimited embedded Metric message), field 3 the sequence
 number.

  SpbPayload = record {
   timestamp : Integer,
   seq : Integer,
   metrics : List SpbMetric
  }

  spb-encode-payload : SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-encode-payload (p) =
   let ts-part = pb-encode-field-varint 1 (p.timestamp)
   in let metrics-part = spb-encode-metrics (p.metrics) 0 (list-length (p.metrics)) []
   in let seq-part = pb-encode-field-varint 3 (p.seq)
   in ts-part & metrics-part & seq-part

  spb-encode-metrics : List SpbMetric, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  spb-encode-metrics (metrics) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else spb-encode-metrics metrics (i + 1) len (acc & pb-encode-field-bytes 2 (spb-encode-metric (list-at metrics i)))

Section: Sequence Number

 The Sparkplug sequence number is a byte that increments on every
 message from an edge node and wraps from 255 back to 0. A birth
 message resets it to 0.

  spb-next-seq : Integer -> Integer
  spb-next-seq (n) = if n >= 255 then 0 else n + 1

Section: Message Builders

 A Sparkplug message is an MQTT PUBLISH at QoS 0 with the encoded
 payload as its body.

  spb-build-node-message : Text, Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-build-node-message (group) (msg-type) (node) (payload) =
   mqtt-build-publish (spb-node-topic group msg-type node) (spb-encode-payload payload) QosAtMostOnce False

  spb-build-device-message : Text, Text, Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-build-device-message (group) (msg-type) (node) (device) (payload) =
   mqtt-build-publish (spb-device-topic group msg-type node device) (spb-encode-payload payload) QosAtMostOnce False

  spb-nbirth : Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-nbirth (group) (node) (payload) = spb-build-node-message group spb-msg-nbirth node payload

  spb-ndata : Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-ndata (group) (node) (payload) = spb-build-node-message group spb-msg-ndata node payload

  spb-ndeath : Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-ndeath (group) (node) (payload) = spb-build-node-message group spb-msg-ndeath node payload

  spb-dbirth : Text, Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-dbirth (group) (node) (device) (payload) = spb-build-device-message group spb-msg-dbirth node device payload

  spb-ddata : Text, Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-ddata (group) (node) (device) (payload) = spb-build-device-message group spb-msg-ddata node device payload

  spb-ddeath : Text, Text, Text, SpbPayload -> List Integer
  spb-ddeath (group) (node) (device) (payload) = spb-build-device-message group spb-msg-ddeath node device payload
